# Full end-to-end QEMU coverage of the appliance ISO installer chain.
#
# Drives internal/le/qemu/install_iso.go, which builds the
# installer initrd + a credential-bearing appliance image, creates a bootable
# ISO via `ze appliance iso --target`, boots that ISO in QEMU against
# two blank disks, asserts the initrd consumes ze.target, writes the embedded
# image without PXE zefs injection, powers off safely, then boots the written
# disk and logs in over SSH using the image's embedded ZeFS credentials.
#
# The installer kernel, QEMU, GRUB rescue tooling, xorriso, static busybox, and
# image-build tooling are environment prerequisites. The driver self-skips with
# a single clear INSTALL-ISO-QEMU: SKIP line when they are absent.

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=./le qemu install-iso-test
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:regex=INSTALL-ISO-QEMU: (PASS|SKIP)
expect=stdout:regex=INSTALL-ISO-QEMU: (SKIP|installer consumed explicit ze.target=/dev/vda)
